# Code owners for this repository.
#
# A pattern listed here requests a review from its owner automatically when a
# pull request touches a matching file. Only real GitHub accounts with access to
# this repository appear below — an unknown or unauthorised username makes the
# whole entry silently do nothing, which is worse than having no CODEOWNERS at
# all because it looks like protection that is not there.
#
# Verified collaborators at the time of writing:
#   @Mohamed-Hamza  @Hamed-mohamed-Git
#
# Note: CODEOWNERS requests a review; it does not require one. Requiring owner
# approval is a separate switch in the branch ruleset, deliberately left off
# while the team is small enough that it would block every merge.

# Default owners for everything not matched more specifically below.
*                       @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything that changes how the application is built, released or deployed.
# A mistake in these files does not fail a test — it fails a deployment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/     @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git
/Dockerfile             @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git
/.dockerignore          @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git
/docker-compose.yml     @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git

# Caddy owns TLS, the SPA fallback and the /api and /uploads proxying. A wrong
# line here means every deep link 404s in production while CI stays green.
/Caddyfile              @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git

# The shared API client carries session, CSRF and error handling for every
# request the application makes.
/src/shared/api/        @Mohamed-Hamza @Hamed-mohamed-Git
